 "graph": {
  "name": "espurna-h",
  "version": "1.0",
  "date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "ESPurna-H v0.8 (Xose Pérez) as published: an ESP-12F (ESP8266) wall switch behind a mains terminal – an HLK-PM01 230 V AC to 5 V module behind a thermal fuse, a 500 mA fuse and an S10K250 varistor, an AMS1117-3.3, a 10 A SRD-05VDC-SL-C relay switched by a 2N7002 with a 1N4148 across its coil, and an HLW8012 power monitor on a 1 mΩ shunt and a 5 × 470 kΩ divider – its GND tied to the line by a 0 Ω resistor, as the HLW8012 requires. Transcribed for edakit's tests.",
  "purpose": {
   "use": "private",
   "market": "EU",
   "notes": "Published as open hardware for experienced makers to build at their own risk (its README); the transcription is a test of edakit, not a product."
  },
  "conventions": {
   "pin_reference": "'<designator>.<pin>' with the pin numbers of the EasyEDA/LCSC symbols – they differ from the Eagle pads where noted in the parts entries (relay: 1/4 coil, 5 common, 2 NO, 3 NC; LL4148: 1 cathode, 2 anode; HLK-PM01: 1 AC_L, 2 AC_N, 3 VO−, 4 VO+)",
   "v": "per net: [min, max] in V against GND over all intended operating states; the mains nets at the peak of 230 V + 10 %",
   "names": "the schematic's net names; its unnamed nets (N$…) named after their function, the Eagle name in notes",
